{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/master/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "pmat",
          "version": "3.30.0",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "PRREV-PRIMARY-001",
              "name": "CUDA context-overflow error mapping left incomplete on adjacent endpoints"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "pmat query \"serving context KV device limit\" --limit 10 --format json ; pmat analyze complexity/tdg/satd (per changed file); scripts/pr_review_duplication_scan.sh --rust-semantic"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "PRREV-PRIMARY-001",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "try_cuda_generate (batch_processing.rs) and try_cuda_batch_generate (batch.rs) hardcode StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR for every error from generate_gpu_resident(), bypassing generation_error_status(). The exact defect class this PR fixes (CUDA context-overflow returning 500 instead of a client 400) still fully reproduces on the /generate and /batch/generate CUDA endpoints, which this diff does not touch. batch.rs already contains a correct pattern (generation_err(), line 85-91, using generation_error_status()) that was not applied to try_cuda_batch_generate.",
            "markdown": "`try_cuda_generate` (batch_processing.rs) and `try_cuda_batch_generate` (batch.rs) hardcode `StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` for every error from `generate_gpu_resident()`, bypassing `generation_error_status()`. The exact defect class this PR fixes (CUDA context-overflow returning 500 instead of a client 400) still fully reproduces on the `/generate` and `/batch/generate` CUDA endpoints, which this diff does not touch. `batch.rs` already contains a correct pattern (`generation_err()`, line 85-91, using `generation_error_status()`) that was not applied to `try_cuda_batch_generate`."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": { "uri": "crates/aprender-serve/src/api/batch_processing.rs" },
                "region": { "startLine": 492, "endLine": 498 }
              }
            }
          ],
          "relatedLocations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": { "uri": "crates/aprender-serve/src/api/batch.rs" },
                "region": { "startLine": 515, "endLine": 521 }
              },
              "message": { "text": "identical hardcoded 500 pattern; contrast with the correct generation_err() wrapper at batch.rs:85-91" }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "measured",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "A CUDA-served client sends a prompt at or past the device KV cache through POST /generate or POST /batch/generate (not /v1/chat/completions or /v1/completions, which this PR fixes). generate_gpu_resident() returns Err(ContextLimitExceeded); try_cuda_generate/try_cuda_batch_generate map ANY error, including this one, to 500 via a literal StatusCode::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, never reaching generation_error_status(). The client again sees an opaque 500 'the server broke' instead of a 400 naming the context limit, on two CUDA endpoints this PR leaves unchanged.",
            "command": "grep -n \"generate_gpu_resident(&prompt_ids, &q_config)\" -A6 crates/aprender-serve/src/api/batch_processing.rs crates/aprender-serve/src/api/batch.rs",
            "exit_code": 0,
            "stdout_sha256": "1b873d70cbaf30f0a88173273aa51e6ffccc8c8d26dca14ccfee203c0ead9244"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "nvidia-cuda-docs",
          "version": "mcp",
          "rules": [
            { "id": "PRREV-CUDA", "name": "device-behaviour claim vs NVIDIA docs" }
          ]
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": [
            {
              "level": "error",
              "message": {
                "text": "nvidia-cuda-docs MCP unreachable: ToolSearch for mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__search_cuda_docs returned no matching deferred tool in this session; only mcp__nvidia-cuda-docs__authenticate / complete_authentication resolved, indicating the server requires an interactive OAuth flow this headless review session cannot complete. authenticate() was deliberately not invoked (it would start a real browser OAuth redirect, inappropriate to trigger unprompted in a review)."
              },
              "properties": { "grounding": "measured" }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "results": []
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "cargo-mutants",
          "version": "27.0.0",
          "rules": [
            { "id": "PRREV-MUTATION", "name": "mutation coverage of the diff" }
          ]
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": false,
          "toolExecutionNotifications": [
            {
              "level": "error",
              "message": {
                "text": "cargo-mutants unreachable in this review: this review runs on the lambda host, which the task's own instructions and this repo's memory rule (feedback_tests_on_intel_never_lambda.md, COP 2026-09-28) forbid running `cargo test`/`cargo nextest` on. cargo-mutants --in-diff internally drives repeated cargo build + cargo test cycles per mutant, so it cannot be run here without violating that constraint. Not attempted; recorded as unreachable rather than a clean run of zero mutants."
              },
              "properties": { "grounding": "measured" }
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "results": []
    },
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "antigravity",
          "version": "1.2.12",
          "rules": [
            { "id": "PRREV-ARM-E", "name": "cross-vendor second-opinion review (advisory)" }
          ]
        }
      },
      "invocations": [
        {
          "executionSuccessful": true,
          "commandLine": "agy --model gemini-3.1-pro-high --dangerously-skip-permissions --print-timeout 30m --output-format json --json-schema .pr-review-schema.json < prompt.txt"
        }
      ],
      "results": [
        {
          "ruleId": "AGY-1",
          "level": "warning",
          "message": {
            "text": "agy (gemini-3.1-pro-high): try_cuda_generate/try_cuda_batch_generate still hardcode 500 for every CUDA generation error, so the 500-on-context-overflow defect this PR fixes on the chat/completions/stream handlers still reproduces on /generate and /batch/generate. (Independently confirmed by the primary reviewer as a measured finding; see the pmat-driver result above.)"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": { "uri": "crates/aprender-serve/src/api/batch_processing.rs" },
                "region": { "startLine": 492 }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "Same failure scenario as the pmat-driver PRREV-PRIMARY-001 result above: a CUDA-served /generate or /batch/generate request past the device KV cache still returns an opaque 500 instead of a 400."
          }
        },
        {
          "ruleId": "AGY-2",
          "level": "note",
          "message": {
            "text": "agy (gemini-3.1-pro-high): confirmed serve_context_refusal() is correctly wired into all three touched CUDA handlers (cuda_chat_backend.rs, gpu_completions_handler.rs, stream_generate.rs) and that generation_error_status() correctly maps ContextLimitExceeded to 400; no defect found on the handlers this diff actually touches."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": { "uri": "crates/aprender-serve/src/api/mod.rs" },
                "region": { "startLine": 392 }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "grounding": "asserted",
            "precision_class": "advisory",
            "failure_scenario": "Confirmatory finding, not a defect: names no failure this diff permits. Recorded as agy_only in the divergence ledger since it does not describe a problem the primary reviewer would independently report as a finding."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
